<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.17.6: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02054</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.17.6: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>b2b0db0c-0c07-4980-aabb-0b6b12518b28</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>

        <exercise id="_2252dcce-e1e0-4a08-b5c2-468676440321" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">

            <para id="para-00002">Here is the graph of quadratic function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00003">Andre uses the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to define <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00004">Noah uses the expression <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> to define <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Do you agree with either of them?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00006">Correct! No. The vertex of the graph is (5,-7). The graph of Andre’s function would have a vertex at (5,7), and the graph of Noah’s function would have a vertex at (-5,-7).</para>
            <para id="para-00007">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00008">The correct answer is No. The vertex of the graph is (5,-7). The graph of Andre’s function would have a vertex at (5,7), and the graph of Noah’s function would have a vertex at (-5,-7).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_282d6d0c-46f8-46a0-badc-fc34c38a8ccd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">

            <para id="para-00009">Here are the graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
            <para id="para-00010">How do the three graphs compare?</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00012">They all have the same vertex.</para>
            <para id="para-00013">The shape is the same but they are in different locations.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">They all have a negative a coefficient in the vertex form of the equation.</para>
            <para id="para-00015">All three graphs contain the point <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00016">Correct! The shape is the same but they are in different locations.</para>
            <para id="para-00017">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">The correct answer is: The shape is the same but they are in different locations.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_44662707-e10a-4387-b777-c39c27a3d344" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00019">Compare the graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What role does the -5 play in the comparison?</para>
            <para id="para-00020">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 5 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00022">Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 5 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00023">Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 5 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00025">Correct! Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00026">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">The correct answer is: Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_72dc86cb-6e3f-4c54-8a83-e694249dc1cd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00028">Compare the graphs of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>. What roles do the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> play in the comparison?</para>
            <para id="para-00029">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00030">Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00031">Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the up by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 8 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00032">Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the right by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 8 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00033">Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the down by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 8 units.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00034">Correct! Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units.</para>
            <para id="para-00035">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.2.</para>
            <para id="para-00036">The correct answer is: Adding 2 to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> before squaring shifts the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_1f55aa1e-b16c-4b06-a84d-cc7775bce93f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00037"><emphasis>Select the three</emphasis> equations with a graph whose vertex has both a positive <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and a positive <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            
            <para id="para-00038">Try again. Revisit activities 7.17.2 – 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00039">The correct answers are: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7667ebf6-4a0e-43ee-ad68-e4122e29fcd1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00040">Which equation represents the graph shown?
          
          <media alt="GRAPH OF A DOWNWARD PARABOLA WITH A VERTEX AT (NEGATIVE 7, 3"><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_19_11_01.jpg"/></media></para>
            <para id="para-00041">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00042"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00043"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00044"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00045"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00046">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00047">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00048">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_9a934902-5287-41e8-9605-420df0d5afb2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00049">The graph representing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is shifted 4 units to the left, 16 units down, and flipped so it opens downward (reflects over the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis). Which equation defines the curve?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00050">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00051">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00052">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_98eb9153-ec2e-4bec-8e61-67ae884326f0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00008">
            <para id="para-00053">The graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> is transformed by a horizontal dilation of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math>. What is the equation of the function that results from this translation?</para>
            <para id="para-00054">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00055"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00056"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00057"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00058"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00008">
            <para id="para-00059">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00060">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00061">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> .</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="e7ef5d3c-1203-48a7-bcbc-cc6e2525319c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            <para id="para-00062">Select the two descriptions that apply.</para>
            <para id="para-00063">A function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> was transformed from the parent quadratic function. Which of the following answer choices describes the transformations that were applied?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00064">Correct! A horizontal dilation by a factor of 2 and A vertical shift down 5 units</para>
            <para id="para-00065">Try again. Revisit activities 7.17.2 – 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00066">The correct answer are: A horizontal dilation by a factor of 2 and A vertical shift down 5 units.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0a126082-3fce-4bb1-afd0-2bbcb81e7ef9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            <para id="para-00067">Which of the following represents a function that has experienced a horizontal compression?</para>
            <para id="para-00068">Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para id="para-00069"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00070"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00071"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00072"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00073">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></para>
            <para id="para-00074">Try again. Revisit activity 7.17.5.</para>
            <para id="para-00075">The correct answer is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mfrac><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> .</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

    </section>
  </content></document>